      origins: "German Whist is a two-player trick-taking game of British origin despite its name. It appears to have originated in England and was popular among diplomats in Vienna in the late 19th century. Rules were first published in London in Home Notes (1894) and in R.F. Foster's Encyclopedia of Games in America (1897).",
